#* {{quote-book|en|year=1893|chapter=Remarks upon the Way from Abingdon to Southamption, and other Places|title=The Manuscripts of His Grace the Duke of Portland|volume=2|location=London|publisher=Her Majesty's Stationery Office|page=288|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=1asKAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA288|text=Here are in these seas two dangerous '''races''', the one called St. Alban's, the other Portland Race.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1980|first=Pauline H.|last=Gurewitz|title=Hydraulic Research in the United States and Canada, 1978|page=120|text=The existing analysis and program for the propeller-rudder interaction has been updated incorporating all the improvements concerned with the propeller loading distribution, including that associated with the fact that the rudder is immersed in the '''race''' of the propeller.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=2003|month=December|first=Jonathan|last=Raban|title=Julia and the Whirlpools|journal=Cruising World|volume=29|number=12|page=40|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=B4AeuY4wnB0C&pg=PA40|text=This is an area of spectacular tidal '''races''', rips, swirls, boils, whirlpools, overfalls, currents, and countercurrents. Scylla and Charybdis pale by comparison with the great maelstroms where the sea is trapped between Vancouver Island and the Canadian mainland.}}
