# A [[guide]] or channel that a [[component]] of a [[machine]] moves along:
## {{lb|en|sewing|weaving}} A [[groove]] on a [[sewing machine]] or a [[loom]] along which the [[shuttle]] moves.
##: {{synonyms|en|shuttle race}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1860|first=Charles|last=Cole|title=The Sewing Machine, and its Capabilities|page=53|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=PiVcAAAAQAAJ&pg=PA53|text=I have lately seen a shuttle machine of Messrs. Grover Baker's construction, in which the shuttle worked in a semi-circular '''race''' and produced two stitches at each revolution of the wheel.}}
##* {{quote-journal|en|date=1872-11-29|title=Improved Loom for Weaving Fabrics of Any Width|journal=The English Mechanic and Word of Science|volume=16|number=401|page=259|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=LrXmAAAAMAAJ&pg=PA259|text=Meanwhile another lug on the shuttle-band engages another carrier at the other end of the loom, and the belt, continuing to move in the same direction, conveys the carrier across the '''race''' in a similar manner as above described.}}
## {{lb|en|engineering}} A [[ring]] with a groove in which rolling elements (such as balls) ride, forming part of a rolling-element [[bearing]] (for example, a [[ball bearing]]).
##* {{quote-book|en|date=1965-08-15|title=Maintenance of Aeronautical Antifriction Bearings|others=NAVWEPS 01-1A-503|publisher=United States Bureau of Naval Weapons|section=section 2|page=5|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=M861fCPQGssC&pg=PA5|text=These bearings do not employ a loading groove or filling slot but utilize an uninterrupted '''race''' groove containing the maximum number of balls that can be introduced by eccentric displacement of the '''races'''.  Due to the relatively large size of the balls and the fact that the ball curvature is only slightly less than the '''race''' curvature, the bearings have comparatively high load carrying capacity in both axial and radial directions.}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1999|first=Steve|last=Goldman|title=Vibration Spectrum Analysis|edition=2nd|publisher=Industrial Press|location=New York|isbn=9780831130886|page=90|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=DtvWhuKHGvwC&pg=PA90|text=The chances of picking up an inner '''race''' fault are small unless the load direction of the bearing coincides with the location of the accelerometer.}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=2017|author=Tian Ran Lin|author2=Kun Yu|author3=Jiwen Tan|chapter=Condition Monitoring and Fault Diagnosis of Roller Element Bearing|doi=10.5772/67143|title=Bearing Technology|editor=Pranav H. Darji|publisher=InTech|location=Rijeka, Croatia|isbn=9789535131830|page=40|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=zvSODwAAQBAJ&pg=PA40|text=The bearing comprises four mechanical components: an outer '''race''', an inner '''race''', rollers (balls), and a cage that holds the rollers (balls) in place.}}
# {{lb|en|gambling}} A [[keno]] [[gambling]] [[session]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2022|first=Kevin|last=Blackwood|first2=Swain|last2=Scheps|chapter=Striking the Mother Lode: Keno and Bingo|title=Casino Gambling For Dummies|edition=2nd|publisher=John Wiley & Sons|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=sl1lEAAAQBAJ&pg=PT293|text=Your odds are sometimes significantly better with video keno {{...}} But because video keno plays so much faster, you're likely to lose more money over a given period. Live keno '''races''' start every 10 minutes, but you can make 100 bets on a video version in the same amount of time.}}

